        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Heat the oven to 190C. Warm the olive oil in a frying pan over a medium heat, add the onion and spring onion and cook for 8 minutes until soft. Transfer to a large bowl."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Wilt the spinach in the same pan with a splash of water, then tip it into a colander. Once cool enough to handle, squeeze out as much liquid as you can, then chop roughly and add to the bowl."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Add the crumbled feta, beaten eggs, parsley, yoghurt if using, and black pepper to the bowl. Mix well. Taste and adjust seasoning, keeping in mind that feta is already salty."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Grease the rectangular baking tin with a little melted butter. Lay sheets of filo pastry into the tin, brushing each sheet generously with melted butter as you go, and letting the edges overhang the sides. Use roughly half the sheets for the base."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Spread the filling evenly over the pastry base. Fold the overhanging edges up over the filling, then layer the remaining filo sheets on top, again brushing each with butter. Tuck the top edges down the sides."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Score the top layers lightly with a sharp knife into portion-sized squares. Brush the top generously with the remaining melted butter."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Bake for 40 to 45 minutes until deep golden and crisp. Allow to rest for 10 minutes before cutting through along the scored lines and serving."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "attrs": {
          "items": [
            {
              "problem": "The base is soggy",
              "solution": "Spinach was not squeezed dry enough. Next time use a clean tea towel to wring out every drop before adding to the filling."
            },
            {
              "problem": "The pastry tears when I lift it",
              "solution": "Filo dries out very fast. Keep unused sheets covered with a damp cloth while you work and handle them quickly."
            },
            {
              "problem": "The top is browning too quickly",
              "solution": "Lay a sheet of foil loosely over the tin after 25 minutes and continue baking until the filling is fully set."
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Where this dish lives"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Spanakopita is one of the most recognisable pies in the Greek kitchen. It is found in bakeries, home kitchens and tavernas across the country. The key to the texture lies in the "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "filo"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "filo pastry"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ", which shatters into flakes with every bite. It travels well and is equally good warm or at room temperature. A wedge of it alongside a simple salad makes a complete lunch."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
